  "summary": "Policy for how an optimization agent should select, order, and stop optimization experiments. Use when optimization stalls: re-derive the whole-system bottleneck and critical path from first principles before choosing scheduling, caching/reuse, or parallelism/pipelining. Covers candidate generation, exploration vs exploitation, diversity, negative experiment memory, budget allocation, and stopping criteria. Drawn from vllm-evolve (phase-locked optimization round), TRT-LLM casebook (prior-art matching), and SkillOpt (bounded edit + gate). Use when deciding what to try next and when to stop.\n",
